TITLE:: RETap
summary:: The hook the recordable reCurrent methods call
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScoreRecorder

DESCRIPTION::
The recordable methods of reCurrent hold one line, code::if(RETap.active) { RETap.action(this, \set, [key, val, seed, quant]) }::: one Boolean check when nothing is armed. Armed recorders register here and every call is forwarded to each of them under link::Classes/RCGuard::, from the main thread only (patterns, control loops and replays run in Routines and are the program's own work). Library code that reaches a recordable method from another one calls its private twin (code::RCBeat.prFree::, code::RCOrgnsm.prRPut::...), so that one action is one event; a subclass specialising a recorded method overrides the twin.

An input opens a cause around its handler: the input is recorded, the actions the handler triggers are not. A code line (the interpreter's code::preProcessor:: and code::codeDump::, installed while a recorder wants code) opens a cause whose actions are recorded as its effects.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: active
True while at least one recorder is armed.

METHOD:: action
argument:: obj
argument:: method
argument:: args
The arguments as called.

METHOD:: input
argument:: kind
code::\midi::, code::\osc:: or code::\keyboard::.
argument:: song
argument:: data
An Event of the fields to record (code::name::, code::raw::, code::value::; code::key::, code::path::, code::args::; code::device::, code::msg::, code::chan::, code::note::, code::value::). code::time:: is not recorded as a field: the recorder stamps the event there when it is a little before now (an OSC bundle's timetag).
argument:: func
The handler, run inside the input's cause; nil records only.
returns:: What func returns.

METHOD:: silently
argument:: func
Nothing is recorded while func runs.

METHOD:: observe
argument:: observer
code::{ |obj, method, args| }::, called for every action func triggers, recorded or not (the taps are active meanwhile; the recorders are not reached when silent).
argument:: func
returns:: What func returns. A replay counts what a code line did before raising, to play only the effects it did not reach.

METHOD:: add
METHOD:: remove
argument:: recorder

METHOD:: enableCode
METHOD:: disableCode
argument:: user
The interpreter hooks are installed while at least one user wants them.

METHOD:: codeHooksInstalled

METHOD:: enableRawMidi
METHOD:: disableRawMidi
argument:: user
MIDIFuncs for every message of every device are installed while at least one user wants them; each message is an input of kind code::\rawMidi::.
METHOD:: rawMidiInstalled
METHOD:: deviceName
argument:: src
The name of a MIDI source by uid ("midi" when unknown).
METHOD:: deviceUid
argument:: name

METHOD:: mainThreadOnly
True by default; false lets tests drive actions from a Routine.

METHOD:: frames
The open causes, innermost last.

METHOD:: beginCode
METHOD:: endCode
Called by the interpreter hooks.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// in a piece that automates with clock-scheduled Functions (they run on the main thread):
clock.sched(1, { RETap.silently { ~beat.set(\amp, 0.2) }; nil });
::
